cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research, please cite it as below."
title: "PHP2Shell — Anatomy of CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619"
abstract: >-
  Technical analysis of the use-after-free in PHP's session layer
  (session.upload_progress) and of the memory corruption via longjmp() on
  OOM, with the real mechanism verified against the PHP 8.2.34 source code,
  a reproducible Docker lab, an exposure detector that reliably discriminates
  between vulnerable and patched versions, and a verified backport of the
  official patch that fixes the flaw without changing the PHP version,
  extensions or ABI.
type: software
